  "description": "CR 607.2d two Obelisks of Urd each pump the creatures of their OWN chosen type",
  "note": "The as-enters creature type read from the affected set's side: Obelisk of Urd's \"Creatures you control of the chosen type get +2/+2\" reaches only the creatures of the type THAT Obelisk chose. Two Obelisks choosing two different types, because one could not tell its own choice apart from \"any chosen type on the battlefield\"; cast rather than placed, so each type is alice's answer as it enters (CR 614.1c). Twelve Plains pay both {6} costs while alice controls no creature, so convoke has nothing to offer; the creatures are cast after. Distinct base sizes so no readings coincide: the Goblin Piker (2/1) is 4/3 under the Goblin Obelisk alone, 6/5 under both and 2/1 under the wrong one; the Elf Dawnhand Dissident (1/2) is 3/4; Darksteel Myr (0/1) is neither type (CR 205.3m) and stays 0/1. The fixture check, both Obelisks on the battlefield, comes last.",
